summary:
  A writer that was stopped before it had a pid starts its ffmpeg all the same.

history:
  The stop signals the pid it finds written down. A writer still
  looking at the stream's first bytes has written none, so the stop takes the
  address file and the writer asks for that file before it starts anything.
  Measured before that: a stop 0.3 s after the start left curl and ffmpeg
  running until the guard's tick.

target:
  package/contents/ui/SlideLogic.js

find:
          + "[ -e " + q(a.cfgPath) + " ] || exit 0; "

replace:
          + ""

expect:
  Killed by tests/qml/tst_slidelogic.qml::test_a_writer_that_was_stopped_while_it_looked_starts_nothing
  and, in the slow set, by tests/test_slide_writer.py::test_a_stop_that_comes_while_the_writer_is_still_looking_leaves_nothing.
